{"Title":"An Act relative to transparency in credit card fees","BillNumber":"S178","DocketNumber":"SD162","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"AMG0","Name":"Anne M. Gobi","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/AMG0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-11T15:36:25.937"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"AMG0","Name":"Anne M. Gobi","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/AMG0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-11T15:36:25.9366667"},{"Id":"JCD1","Name":"James C. Arena-DeRosa","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JCD1","ResponseDate":"2023-09-26T13:07:34.37"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S178/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Ms. Gobi, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 178) of Anne M. Gobi for legislation relative to transparency in credit card fees.  Consumer Protection and Professional Licensure.","DocumentText":"\tSection 28A in Chapter 14D of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2022 Official Edition, is hereby amended by striking out section (2) and inserting in place thereof the following section:- \r\n\t(2) A seller in any sales transaction who imposes a surcharge on a cardholder who elects to use a credit card in lieu of payment by cash, check, or similar means shall inform the purchaser of the surcharge by a sign conspicuously posted on the seller’s premises.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J17","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J17"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}